this morning i was scrolling twitter and  i saw a tweet that had me stopped in my  tracks as i was scrolling through here's  the tweet that i saw turkey is fighting  consumer price inflation by having  authorities go to supermarkets check  prices and threaten fines if the prices  are too high i literally couldn't  believe this so of course everyone knows  that turkey is experiencing incredibly  high inflation right now the estimations  for december is that inflation is going  to come in at a 30  year-over-year change that is insane the  estimations are anywhere between 26 to  37 and the average of all the economists  together is 30 here in the united states  we have almost 7 percent and people are  freaking the hell out imagine if we had  30 well that is what the turkish  citizens and business owners are dealing  with but to add salt to the wound here  is what the local authorities are doing  this is a video that they released  themselves and i'll read to you in a  minute what exactly the tweet says in  translation but let's watch the video  first the local authorities released  this and they are proud of what they are  doing here  this is the authorities  in the grocery store  talking to the grocery store owners  about what the prices of the goods and  services actually are  they not only are  talking to them  they not only  are lecturing them  but they are even going as far as doling  out fines and you'll see they're  scanning prices and they're writing them  down to come back later and check to see  what is the actual increase  and here it goes the crazy part where  you start to see them actually checking  item by items of what the prices are  every single item must be checked must  be written down  it's not just pen and paper  scanning  is that price gouging is a common claim  when high inflation happens governments  step in and they start yelling and  screaming at the business owners and  saying oh it's not the undisciplined  monetary and fiscal policy decisions  we've made instead it is simply that  these business owners are taking  advantage of you but grocery stores  operate on razor thin margins usually  less than five percent profit margins  it's not like in 2021 they just decided  you know what this is the year i'm gonna  price gouge no of course not they have  material costs that are going up the  supply chain is forcing their costs up  and their labor costs are going up as  well it's all tied back to inflation and  so whether they're going to either  operate at a loss or they're going to  increase their prices and pass on those  higher costs to the customer of course  they're going to increase the prices and  so ultimately when you have government  starting to intervene in the market  whether they're implementing some sort  of price control like in turkey or  they're implementing capital controls  where investors can't actually take  their money out of a currency it simply  exasperates the problem so when i see  this video all it tells me is that we  haven't learned from history it is  insane to think of the local police or  local authorities going grocery store by  grocery store by grocery store and  checking every single item to see what  the price is how much it's increased  over time and then issuing fines if you  increase it too much i don't know about  you but i would much rather have  entrepreneurs and business owners  running these businesses than the  government and the local police the  local police was so good at running  businesses maybe they shouldn't be  police officers and instead they should  own businesses but until that day comes  let's leave the businesses to the  business owners and let's leave the  policing to the police
 

